{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1141892-question-about-realms","id":1141892,"title":"Question about Realms","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-09-19T14:11:33-07:00","id":1141892,"title":"Question about Realms","content":"I have a few questions about Realms &amp; their application.<br /> <br /> -On page 194 about Cantrips it says that a changeling might affect different type of target using different Realms, but there is nothing in the side bar for the added difficulty of using additional Primary realms?<br /> Unless the increased difficulty mentioned is due to the fact that you have to use the lowest realm for your dice pool?<br /> <br /> -If I'm using Scene in addition to let's say Fae 1, do I automatically target all the commoners in the Area, or only the one I want???<br /> <br /> -Is it possible to use several level of one realm to affect different target? Would it increase the difficulty?<br /> For example if the motley is composed of commoners / nobles / Gallains (or any 2 of these), can I use Fae 1, 2 &amp; 4 in one casting (in addition to Scene of course)?<br /> <br /> -What about time, can I use Time 1, 3 &amp; 4 (for example) in one casting?<br /> <br /> I would probably allow all of these, but I find the rules a little lacking there (unless I missed something which would be entirely possible as I didn't had the time to do a proper thorough reading yet)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5462-kendaan","name":"Kendaan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T19:52:55-07:00","id":1142006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kendaan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1141892-question-about-realms#post1141892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a few questions about Realms &amp; their application.<br /> <br /> -On page 194 about Cantrips it says that a changeling might affect different type of target using different Realms, but there is nothing in the side bar for the added difficulty of using additional Primary realms?<br /> Unless the increased difficulty mentioned is due to the fact that you have to use the lowest realm for your dice pool?</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't remember in C20, but in 2nd Ed it would be +1 difficulty per extra Realm used.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> -If I'm using Scene in addition to let's say Fae 1, do I automatically target all the commoners in the Area, or only the one I want??? </div> </div> </div>If you're only affecting a single changeling there is no reason to add Scene. If you did want to affect multiple ones I would personally rule that everyone in that area was affected, but you don't have to affect the WHOLE area described by that level of Scene.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> -Is it possible to use several level of one realm to affect different target? Would it increase the difficulty?<br /> For example if the motley is composed of commoners / nobles / Gallains (or any 2 of these), can I use Fae 1, 2 &amp; 4 in one casting (in addition to Scene of course)?<br /> <br /> -What about time, can I use Time 1, 3 &amp; 4 (for example) in one casting? </div> </div> </div>I've always ruled that you use the highest level of Realm necessary. So in the case of the commoner, noble, and Gallain motley, you would use Fae 4 + Scene. Remember that the level of Realm is not ONLY that level, but all of the levels up to it. So a level 3 Realm could affect everything in levels 1-3.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://imgbb.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://image.ibb.co/fzeOgQ/1172c70f3ff188688852c74c8145285c_original_2_4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> Visit my freehold for Changeling links, settings, art, and other goodies.<br /> <a href=\"https://theshepherdsfreehold.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The Shepherd's Freehold</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13648-shepherd","name":"Shepherd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}